                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and require distinct valid roots on the two branches.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Replacing $x$ with $x-h$ gives $f(x-h)=|x-h-2|$, with vertex $(h+2,0)$.\n\nFor $x\\leq h+2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}h+2-x&=\\frac{x}{2}-2\\\\x&=\\frac{2h+8}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nThis root satisfies $x\\leq h+2$ exactly when $h\\geq2$.\n\nFor $x\\geq h+2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x-h-2&=\\frac{x}{2}-2\\\\x&=2h.\\end{align*}$$\nThis root satisfies $x\\geq h+2$ exactly when $h\\geq2$.\n\nWhen $h=2$, both roots are $x=4$. When $h>2$, the roots are distinct and lie on opposite sides of the vertex. Therefore, two intersections occur exactly when $h>2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 94
